<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dimensions for the Android TV subscription transfer (module: tv).

  A separate file for the same reason `strings_tv.xml` is one — the TV screens are a
  self-contained pair and `dimens.xml` is edited by everyone. It follows the
  `dimens_onboarding.xml` precedent, not a second spacing scale: everything a phone
  screen needs still comes from `dimens.xml`, and nothing here is reachable from one.

  These are TELEVISION constants, not tokens on the 4dp ramp:

  · OVERSCAN. A TV crops the edges of the panel; the safe area is about 90% of it.
    These two sit OUTSIDE the 16dp screen gutter, so the pairing card ends up 40dp
    from the physical edge and no control can be cropped off the panel.
  · THE PAIRING QR is sized for a phone camera two metres away, which is what makes
    it a fixed 320dp square and not a fraction of the card.
-->
<resources>

    <dimen name="tv_overscan_horizontal">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_overscan_vertical">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_pairing_qr">320dp</dimen>

</resources>
